  "readmeFile": "docs\\README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.0.7-alpha (2026-11-14) - 2 new nodes, 66 in all. GeometryEditor (NetTopologySuite.Geometry):\n      a geometry drawn by hand. Select the node and press Ctrl+Shift+W: a window opens with tools for\n      points, lines, polygons with holes, rectangles and circles, box selection, undo and redo, and\n      snapping. The drawing is written into the node's WKT pin, so it is saved with the patch as text.\n      SetSRID (NetTopologySuite.Geometry): says which coordinate system a geometry's numbers are in,\n      and moves nothing. GeometryEditor has an SRID pin too; with SRID 4326 the window and the drawn\n      Geometry IOBox show longitude and latitude at their true proportions, and the window names the\n      CRS and its units. With VL.PROJ installed, any EPSG code is named. New help patches: HowTo Draw\n      a geometry, HowTo Draw in longitude and latitude, HowTo Say which CRS a geometry is in.\n\n      0.0.6-alpha (2026-11-08) - 8 new nodes, 64 in all. Shapes by position and size, the way VL.Skia\n      describes them: Rectangle (Position, Width, Height, Anchor), Rectangle (Join Points), Circle,\n      Ellipse, RegularPolygon, Arc, Sector (NetTopologySuite.Geometry). Coordinates are a map's: y\n      grows north, so the TopLeft anchor is the north-west corner. Angles in cycles. New help patch\n      HowTo Make a shape. Coordinate (FromVector2): a position from a mouse, Skia or Stride\n      becomes a coordinate, losing nothing; positions stay coordinates (double). 64 nodes.\n      A drawn Geometry IOBox now keeps its view while you edit, so a wider rectangle looks wider\n      and a bigger circle bigger; a dot grid and a label like 4 × 2 · grid 1 give the real size.\n      BREAKING: Read WKT and Write WKT are now FromWKT and ToWKT, in the same category, with no\n      alias - a patch made with an older version shows the old node unresolved; put FromWKT or\n      ToWKT in its place. Named after what you get, the way VL names FromHSL or ToString.\n\n      0.0.5-alpha (2026-11-08) - 16 new nodes, 56 in all. Tier 1 of the coverage plan:\n      Touches, Crosses, Overlaps, Covers, CoveredBy, Relate, IsWithinDistance, SymmetricDifference,\n      ConvexHull, Reverse (NetTopologySuite.Operation); Envelope, InteriorPoint, Boundary, IsSimple,\n      NumPoints (NetTopologySuite.Geometry). And Outlines (NetTopologySuite.Geometry): one polyline\n      per ring or line, and every point. A Geometry now draws itself in the editor the way a GIS\n      draws it: hover a Geometry pin or make an IOBox of one and you see filled polygons with their\n      holes, lines, point markers, a map pin for a point, a Feature with every attribute listed under\n      it (VL.NetTopologySuite.HDE.vl, editor only). Every help patch shows its geometry that way;\n      new help patch HowTo Wrap points in a hull, six patches extended.\n\n      0.0.4-alpha (2026-10-18) - Tooltips rewritten to be short: every node now shows a one-line\n      summary, a sentence or two of usage and a line per pin on hover, instead of design notes.\n      No node changed. Same 40 nodes as 0.0.3-alpha.\n\n      0.0.3-alpha (2026-10-18) - Adds GetAttribute (NetTopologySuite.Feature): one\n      attribute by name, with Success instead of an exception. VL.NetTopologySuite.GeoJSON (formerly\n      VL.GeoJSON) depends on this version.\n\n      0.0.2-alpha (2026-10-17) - The nodes now live under NetTopologySuite.Geometry, .Operation, .IO,\n      .Feature, .Index and .Network instead of NTS.*, so searching the NodeBrowser for the package's\n      own name finds them. Patches made with 0.0.1-alpha keep working: a node resolves by name\n      within the referenced package. Also: Test-Install -FromNuGetOrg, and the README's install\n      section. No node added, removed or changed.\n\n      0.0.1-alpha (2026-09-26) - The first release, a prerelease. 39 nodes in six categories - NTS.Geometry,\n      NTS.Feature, NTS.Operation, NTS.IO, NTS.Index, NTS.Network - 126 tests, 15 help patches, and\n      F1 on every node opens one. Verified in vvvv gamma 7.4. Coordinates are copied on the way in\n      and out, so a geometry cannot be moved behind your back. Not ready for real work: the node\n      surface may still change between prereleases.",
